  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Monday)\nIssued at 930 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThursday night will have seasonable lows around 70 degrees under \npartly cloudy skies. On Friday, the ridge to our west will expand \nand provide an increase in heat concerns that will persist through\nthe weekend. Otherwise, there's a low to medium chances (20-40%) \nfor diurnal showers and thunderstorms with the greatest coverage \neast of I-65. This weekend, moisture will wrap around the western \nside of the subtropical ridge out in the Atlantic and bring an \nincrease in rainfall, low to medium (30-60%) chances Saturday \nthrough Monday. Highest coverage will again be east of I-65. Highs\nwill be in the upper 80s to lower 90s Friday through Monday but \nheat index values will push above 100 degrees. At this time, \nvalues remain just below Heat Advisory criteria however trends \nwill be monitored. Regardless, practice heat safety!",
